Flexural strength tests were conducted on prism specimens of 100*100*500 mm according to IS 516. After a 24-h casting time, the specimens were demolded and water-cured until the specified testing age. A two-point loading design was used to provide loads at one-third of the span in order to give a constant bending moment in the centre section. When the load was gradually applied until it failed, the ultimate load was recorded. The flexural strength (modulus of rupture) is calculated by using Eq. ( 2 ). The test’s goal was to ascertain how basalt fibres impacted the flexural performance, crack resistance, post-cracking behaviour, and load-carrying capacity of high-strength concrete . 2 \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
