The procedures described in IS 5816 were used to measure the tensile strength of concrete using cylindrical specimens of 150 mm in diameter and 300 mm in height. Specimens were placed in the testing apparatus following the recommended curing time, and a load was applied along its longitudinal diameter until failure occurred. The specimen developed a vertical crack and eventually split because of the tensile stresses created due to the applied compressive force that were perpendicular to the loading direction. The specimen’s maximum load at the moment of failure was noted, and tensile strength is calculated using the conventional relationship shown in Eq. ( 3 ). The purpose of the test was to check the tensile performance of basalt fiber-reinforced concrete and investigate the role that both macro and micro basalt fibres play in strengthening resistance to tensile loads and stopping the spread of cracks. 3 \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
